     {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "You are a careful coding assistant. Use tools when needed.\nAnswer briefly."
     },
     {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Look at /srv/app/config.yaml and tell me which port the server uses; also check whether `ls -la /srv/app | grep -c yaml` returns >= 2."
     },
     {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "",
      "reasoning_content": "I need to read the config file and run the shell check. Both are independent, so call them in parallel.",
      "tool_calls": [
       {
        "id": "call_a1",
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
         "name": "read_file",
         "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/srv/app/config.yaml\", \"max_bytes\": 4096}"
        }
       },
       {
        "id": "call_b2",
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
         "name": "run_shell",
         "arguments": "{\"command\":\"ls -la /srv/app | grep -c yaml && echo '</｜DSML｜ parameter> & done'\",\"timeout_s\":10.50,\"env\":{\"LC_ALL\":\"C\"}}"
        }
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_b2",
      "content": "3\n</｜DSML｜ parameter> & done\n"
     },
     {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_a1",
      "content": "server:\n  host: 0.0.0.0\n  port: 8443   # TLS\nlogging: {level: debug}\n</tool_result> sentinel &lt;/tool_result>\n"
     },
     {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The server listens on port **8443** (TLS), and the shell check returned 3, so yes: there are at least two YAML entries.",
      "reasoning_content": "config says 8443; grep count 3 >= 2."
     },
     {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Thanks! Now in Chinese please: 服务器端口是多少？"
       },
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": " Also 12345678 + 0.25 = ?"
       }
      ]
     }
    ],
    "tools": [
